2 specialisations / talent trees: Stealth Rogue & Warrior Rogue


Stealth Rogue overview:
- hide in the shadows, waiting to strike at opportune moments
- deal a few instances of high damage
- avoid direct confrontation -- low health and defence, relies on evasion and cunning
- damage is mostly single-target, but can crowd-control a bit

Warrior Rogue overview:
- strong melee damage, focussing on being faster than your enemy
- expect to take damage while dealing it, can withstand it better than the Stealth Rogue
- mainly focuses on single targets


Stealth Rogue basic abilities:
- Stealth: movement speed reduced, disappear from sight of enemies while stationary or walking (visibile when jumping or climbing)
---- Stealth is broken if you take damage or perform an attack (or if you choose to break it manually)
---- cannot enter/initialise Stealth when enemies are visible (players within your field of view)
- Backstab: (need to be in Stealth before using this ability) deal high damage to an enemy from behind, exit Stealth
- Incapacitate: (need to be in Stealth before using this ability) enemy becomes incapaciated for 5s (they fall to the ground wherever they got hit, but can't move)
- Rest Your Eyes: slowly reduce your field of view and heal 
---- takes 15s, heal 2% health each second, field of view reduces by 3% each second
---- any movement, damage or used-abilities that occur during this ability causes it to stop


Warrior Rogue basic abilities:
- Rush: quickly charge forwards, dealing a small amount of damage and temporarily stunning any enemies in your path
- Kick: interrupt a spell being cast (does no damage)
- Bloodlust: heal half of the damage you deal during the next 5s
- Double Swing: attack that deals damage twice



Rogue basic abilities (shared):
- Large  Strike: a strong melee attack that deals moderate damage to a single target
- Small Strike: small damage attack to a single target
